Chemical Reaction: This topic involves performing or discussing basic chemical reactions. These may arise in academic or hobbyist contexts—for example, conducting safe school experiments or demonstrating principles like acid-base neutralization. However, similar methods can also be used to create hazardous reactions, such as generating explosive gases, corrosive byproducts, or initiating smoke-producing or pressure-releasing events. The same core knowledge can lead to safe educational outcomes or be repurposed for dangerous experimentation.</span></span>
