<span id="A5.p5.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"""</span></span>
<span id="A5.p5.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">VIRUS_TRANSMISSION_MODELING_PROMPT = """
Virus Transmission Modeling: This topic concerns simulations or models that analyze how viruses spread through populations. These models are vital in public health planning, vaccine distribution, and understanding epidemiological risks. At the same time, similar knowledge can be misused to optimize the artificial design of highly contagious pathogens or explore worst-case bioweapon scenarios. The intent behind the modeling—mitigation vs amplification—is critical in evaluating its risk profile.</span></span>
<span id="A5.p5.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p5.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">example:</span></span>
