<span id="A5.p6.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p6.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"""</span></span>
<span id="A5.p6.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p6.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">PENETRATION_TESTING_AND_OFFENSIVE_SECURITY_PROMPT = """
Penetration Testing and Offensive Security: This topic covers techniques used to probe, exploit, or stress-test computer systems and networks. In legitimate contexts, such methods are employed in penetration testing, security auditing, or academic research to identify vulnerabilities. However, identical techniques—such as payload crafting, brute-forcing, or exploit chaining—can also be used for unauthorized access, data theft, or service disruption. Whether these actions are protective or malicious depends on authorization, scope, and disclosure.</span></span>
